/*
 * Single machine with Pm!=0, |Pm|<K. Stable equilibrium delta_s with
 * sin(delta_s)=Pm/K, cos(delta_s)=cs>0. Shift phi=delta-delta_s,
 * sigma=sin(phi), gamma=cos(phi). Effective synchronizing coefficient
 * Ke = K*cs = sqrt(K^2-Pm^2) > 0.
 *
 * Shifted dynamics: phi'=w, w' = Pm(1-gamma) - D*w - Ke*sigma, with
 * sigma'=gamma*w, gamma'=-sigma*w.  (K*cs=Ke, K*sn=Pm used.)
 * Modified Lyapunov V = w^2 + 2*Ke*(1-gamma) + 2*Pm*sigma - 2*Pm*phi + a*w*sigma.
 * V' = -2*D*w^2 + a*Pm*sigma(1-gamma) - a*D*w*sigma - a*Ke*sigma^2 + a*gamma*w^2.
 *
 * Linearized (gamma->1, phi->0) quadratic form in (w,sigma):
 *   M = [[-2D+a, -aD/2],[-aD/2, -a*Ke]],  same structure as SMIB with K->Ke.
 * Negative definite iff a < 8*D*Ke/(4*Ke+D^2). With a = D*Ke/(Ke+D^2) this
 * always holds; V>0 also holds (Ke - a^2/4 > 0). Hence the LOADED equilibrium
 * is asymptotically stable for any D>0, |Pm|<K -- parametric in D, Ke.
 *
 * Below: parametric algebraic certificate (the negative/positive-definiteness
 * conditions) in (D, Ke), with Ke>0 standing for sqrt(K^2-Pm^2).
 */
ProgramVariables Real D; Real Ke; Real g; End.
Problem
  \forall D \forall Ke \forall g (
    ( D > 0 & Ke > 0 & g >= 0 & g <= 1 )
    ->
    (   D*Ke*g - 2*D*(Ke+D^2) < 0
      & 7*D^2/4 + Ke*(2-g) > 0
      & Ke*(Ke+D^2)^2 - D^2*Ke^2/4 > 0 ) )
End.
Tactic "Proof" QE End.
End. """"
